WEBVTT

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:08.290
Man, I'm beat. That last question on
the math test was totally unfair.

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.500
Yeah, it was super difficult.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.830
Huh? Really?

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.700
Maki, you know-it-all!

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:16.330
Hey, what's up?

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.540
Good afternoon.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:18.950
Good job surviving the tests.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.200
Thanks.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.750
I hope I did well enough on the other subjects to cover my ass...

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.750
Hi there.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:26.000
Hello.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.290
I've been thinking...

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:32.040
I want to find a way to make myself look at her...

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.200
...the same way that she always looks at me.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.500
Planned Student Council Activities
East Tomi High School Duty Roster

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.540
Okay.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:17.910
The midterms just ended and council meetings will
officially resume next week, so let's call it a day.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.000
Good idea, let's wrap it up.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.950
Thank you very much!

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.830
Nanami-senpai.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:30.000
How are preparations coming along with
the Student Council Stage Show?

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.790
About that...

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:34.580
We're having problems with the script.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.200
Are we supposed to write the script ourselves?

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.160
The old Student Council used to ask the members
of our Literature Club to write it, but...

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.620
these days they focus only on reading and
none of them has the skill to write for us.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.410
That really sucks.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:52.330
If we can't find anyone to write it, we'll probably
just end up reusing one of the old scripts.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.830
I would prefer to do something
completely original, though.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.410
Say, do any of you know someone
who is good at writing?

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.580
Nah, nobody I know comes to mind.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:04.870
Same here.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:05.910
Koito-san?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:12.040
I-I can't think of anyone...

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.250
Catch y'all later!

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:15.450
See you tomorrow.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.750
Oh, I need to go take care of something, bye!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.500
All locked up?

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.700
Yeah.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.080
I actually know... the perfect person.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:38.540
Putting aside the fact that she's a close friend,
I thought Koyomi's novel was really good.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:43.330
I think she would be more than capable
of writing a script, too.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.870
If she wrote the script for us,
I would actually want to see the show.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.330
But...

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.620
I thought you had something to take care of?

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.370
S..Saeki-senpai!

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.120
Is that a novel?

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.700
Didn't you leave together with Nanami-senpai?

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:04.080
Nope, we live in totally different directions.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.370
But this is perfect.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.580
I've been meaning to speak with you, Koito-san.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:16.830
Did you write that yourself?

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:21.700
No, a friend wrote it and then asked me to read it over.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:23.910
Oh? And how was it?

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.080
It was interesting.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:33.910
So, you knew someone that could write our script,
but kept it a secret from everyone earlier?

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.330
I'm sorry.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.160
Why didn't you say something?

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:43.120
You don't have to worry,
we aren't going to pressure anyone into it.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.410
It's because...

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.870
You're worried about Touko?

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:53.080
What are you talking about?

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.200
What reason would I have to worry about Nanami-senpai?

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.000
She's willing to do whatever it takes,
even being the lead actress.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.870
That's true. Touko is capable of putting on
a flawless performance, just like she always does.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:06.910
As if.

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:10.750
Did you think I was gullible enough to actually buy that?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.580
Saeki-senpai?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.540
I'm always by her side, so I know everything.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.000
Planned Student Council Activities (Second Semester)

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:25.450
Touko constantly puts up a front of
strength and confidence, but

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.370
in reality she deals with a lot of pressure
from being on the council.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.540
But that's exactly what she wants.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:36.200
Being the Student Council President
and doing the stage show.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.330
Those are things that she decided for herself.

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.040
And yet, you're going to ignore that fact...

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.290
...and just stand in her way?

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:49.000
Hanazawa Publishing Amateur Contest Entry
Title Undecided

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:48.790
But...

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:51.750
why do we have to do a stage show?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.540
The Student Council President from seven years ago...

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:58.830
Huh?

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.870
That's the reason why Touko is
so wrapped up in the stage show.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:03.830
Why don't you find out for yourself?

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.450
Saeki-senpai, do you...

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:11.250
Do you never have any worries about Nanami-senpai?

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:14.080
There's nothing that you need to worry about.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:18.290
She's got me to look after her.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.040
Hey, aren't you going to eat?

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.750
No, I have something I need to do.

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.450
You two go ahead and eat without me.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.450
Did you forget something?

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.870
Yes. I'll come right back after I get it.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:56.250
If this is five years ago, then...
This must be six years ago...

00:06:53.790 --> 00:06:57.830
41st Student Council
39th Student Council

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:09.370
Someone clearly removed them for a specific reason,
but only the documents from seven years ago.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.120
The Student Council President from seven years ago...

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.500
That's the reason why Touko is
so wrapped up in the stage show.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:20.910
Does that mean Nanami-senpai is the one responsible?

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:27.910
Sorry, it totally slipped my mind.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.500
You should have just said something.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.410
The midterms just ended, and besides,
I did tell you that I wasn't in a hurry.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:35.580
I read the whole thing.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:37.200
What did you think?

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:39.540
Good. It was really interesting.

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:44.290
After I finished, I felt the urge to read it again,
so I started over and went through it a second time.

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:45.700
Really?

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.830
Yep. I would really enjoy reading
more of your writing, Koyomi.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.160
That's such a relief.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.160
Were you really that stressed out about it?

00:07:55.790 --> 00:07:59.830
I think getting the honest opinion of an avid reader
is the scariest part of the whole process.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.580
I don't really consider myself an "avid reader".

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:07.330
You are. Out of everyone I know, you're
the only one with an eye for good books.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.910
That's why I trust your opinion the most, Yuu.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:16.910
Hanazawa Publishing Amateur Contest Entry
Title Undecided

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:11.790
I see.

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.950
Koyomi, do you have any interest in stage shows?

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:17.790
Huh?

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:22.080
Oh, not acting, I'm talking about the script.
Maybe writing one?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:23.450
Do you know of an opportunity?

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:26.370
Well, to be honest, I'm not sure yet.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:29.450
There might be one, and there might not be one.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:35.660
I've never written a script, but I'm definitely
interested in writing in a variety of forms.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.700
Okay.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:46.250
I have to do more digging first.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:51.000
I don't want to make any promises to Koyomi now,
only to backtrack later.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.660
Did you find it?

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:54.450
No, not yet.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.040
What exactly are you looking for?

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:01.700
Huh? Um, the Student Council documents
from seven years ago.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.370
Seven years ago, huh?

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.080
None here?

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:11.700
Nope.

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:15.330
Fujishiro Bookstore

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.830
Seriously? Even the records in
the main building are missing?

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.950
But... why?

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:27.750
Maybe it was...

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.870
That's not true.
That can't be true.
I feel for you....
There's something I want
to ask you about...

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.370
I just can't bring myself to ask her directly.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:45.660
I'm home!

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.410
Oh, welcome home.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:51.660
Mom will throw a fit if she finds you using
your phone while on shop duty.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.330
I know.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:56.660
Rei-chan.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:57.620
What?

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:03.330
You mentioned to me once that one of your coworkers
was a former graduate of our school, right?

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:04.910
Yeah, and?

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.080
How old are they?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:11.700
I think they are three years older than me,
so 24 years-old, probably.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:17.200
Got a reply.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:18.540
What does it say?

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.910
The president back then was...

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.160
I'm pretty sure the president back then was Mio Nanami.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.700
"Nanami"...

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.200
So, are they related?

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:38.450
Yeah, Mio Nanami is Touko Nanami's older sister.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:43.620
B-but I remember her saying that she had no siblings.

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.580
Well, that's true now...

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.540
Her sister passed away in a traffic accident.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.750
It happened seven years ago,
just before the culture festival.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:11:00.200
She was idolized by everyone, and even
we teachers relied upon her from time to time.

00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:04.410
She a really great Student Council President,
always at the center of everything.

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.830
So, the Student Council's Stage Show...?

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:11.450
When Nanami's sister died, it was called off.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:16.080
From that year onward, it was never performed again.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:21.580
Nanami is actually exactly like her sister,
it's almost as if they were twins.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.250
That's not true.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.450
They were probably nothing alike.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.450
Senpai is far from perfect,
and very timid on the inside, so...

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:38.660
But one day, I just couldn't do that anymore.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:43.410
I used to be nothing, and I can't go back to that.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:49.410
She ended up this way by trying
to become what her sister had been.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.580
Being the Student Council President
and doing the stage show.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.910
Those are things that she decided for herself.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:12:00.700
Obviously, she's doing all of this because
she wants to and plans to keep going.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:03.540
But...

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:08.750
...for how long?

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:13.160
Senpai.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:15.370
Would you like to walk home together today?

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.040
Huh? S-sure.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:22.200
There's something...

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.000
...I'd like to talk about.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:31.000
Words Kept Repressed

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.160
Want to stop for a drink?

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.620
We're almost at the corner where we have to split up...

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.040
I know.

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:02.500
Want to keep walking?

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.290
Yeah.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.500
It's been a long time since I've come here.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.160
Let's keep walkin-

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:21.080
Nanami-senpai, you're trying
to become exactly like your sister, right?

00:13:27.830 --> 00:13:30.790
I asked a teacher at school about your older sister.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.790
I'm sorry for prying.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:35.410
I see.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:43.450
I figured there must be people who still knew,
even though I tried to keep it hidden.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.950
The reason you want to do the stage show is...

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:54.870
Yes. I'm going to finish what
my sister never got the chance to.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:13:59.790
Um...

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:08.830
Would you consider quitting?

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:13.950
I think it's better if you stay the way you are, Senpai.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:23.700
I think it's reasonable, and even respectable, that
you want to become a person as great as your sister.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.580
But you're pushing yourself too hard to do it.

00:14:27.330 --> 00:14:28.540
It makes me worry.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.250
You don't have to be someone else,

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:37.790
I think there are more people than you realize
who can accept the real you.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:43.500
And I know there are people who
will have affection for the real you, too.

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.080
Because...

00:14:49.370 --> 00:14:55.700
Because I already know the real you
and I still want to stay by your side.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.040
I want to fall in love with you.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:05.200
I would rather die...

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.500
...than hear those words.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.500
Everyone loved my big sister.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.620
I loved her, too.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:35.750
I struggled to believe it when she died,
I just couldn't accept it.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.000
How terrible. She was such a wonderful girl.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:45.040
Touko-chan, you have to keep your head up
and live on for your sister's sake.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.120
Your sister would want that.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.660
Become as outstanding as Mio-chan was.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.500
Live enough for the both of you.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.450
Just like my sister...

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:08.330
I started to think about becoming
a replacement for my sister.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:13.290
When I adopted my sister's persona,
everyone seemed happier.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.580
They even started to call me special.

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:20.330
I'll admit that it feels good to return
to my real self in front of you, but...

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:24.200
...I just can't give up being "special"
in front of everyone else.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:31.080
I understand that it makes
you worry about me, but I'm sorry.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:33.410
We're doing the stage show.

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:36.950
Regardless of whether you decide
to participate or not, Koito-san.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:40.160
Senpai!

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.080
To be honest...

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:55.500
...I thought she would be convinced by what I had to say.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:59.790
Because I know she doesn't want to leave my side.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:12.660
But if I can't be with her,
who else is there for me to learn to love?

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.200
I won't let her go.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:19.540
Don't pretend you're not lonely!

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:25.000
If you weren't lonely, then you wouldn't
be pursuing a relationship.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:32.750
Even though you can't decide between
your weak side and your "perfect" side,

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.870
you still want to be with someone.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:38.700
And that person is me, right?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:48.950
Nanami-senpai, I can't fall in love with either side of you.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.250
I haven't yet.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:53.790
And likely never will.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:02.500
I just can't bring myself... to feel that way about you.

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:08.830
Really?

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:18.160
Will you still stay with me?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:24.830
I already told you, if you ask me
to stay by your side, then that's what I'll do.

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:29.830
I just need you to tell me what it is that you really want.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.330
Nanami-senpai.

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:37.910
I want you... to help with the show.

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:39.950
Okay.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.620
Be by my side.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:43.080
Okay.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.790
When I'm lonely, let me lean on you!

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:46.790
Okay.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.370
Don't have feelings for anyone else!

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:52.200
And don't let your feelings toward me became hate!

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.290
Okay.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.120
And also, Yuu...

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:58.910
Yes?

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:02.250
Please don't...

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:13.330
Just for today, can we hold hands while we walk?

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.250
If that's what you want.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.500
This is a little embarrassing, though.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:26.330
Nobody is even going to notice.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:29.750
Yuu.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.370
I love you.

00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:35.290
Oh... Thank you very much.

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:37.620
Don't change the way you are.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:41.830
I want to change.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:44.040
Okay.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:48.000
Yet, the reason I lied to her was...

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.790
...because I'm also lonely.

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:15.830
This is a little embarrassing, though.

00:22:15.830 --> 00:22:18.370
Nobody is even going to notice.

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:23.080
"Love" is a violent word.

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:31.160
If I love her the way she is now, then it means I would
stop feeling that way if she ever changed. Right?

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:35.540
"Love" is a word that shackles us.

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.200
However, that special feeling... I don't understand it.

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:52.000
The reason I thought she'd be the nicest person
in the world, is precisely because she can't "love".

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:53.750
Because...

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:57.040
I think I'm falling in love with you.

00:22:58.330 --> 00:23:01.620
In reality, Yuu is an incredibly kind person.

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:06.790
She accepts every part of me,
and agrees to stay by my side.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.620
Once I experienced that level of comfort,

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:15.830
I could never go back to being alone again.

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:18.290
Yuu.

00:23:18.870 --> 00:23:19.910
I love you.

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:23.620
Oh... Thank you very much.

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:25.580
These words are shackles.

00:23:26.830 --> 00:23:28.660
Don't change the way you are.

00:23:31.200 --> 00:23:32.330
Please, Yuu.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:41.000
Words Used to Repress

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:38.540
Never fall in love with me.
